
====================================================================================================
S1. The identity that fixes h's argument, and the size of the error
====================================================================================================
  mu_fw(sqrt(y^2+y)) * sqrt(y^2+y) simplifies to: y
  [OK] mu_fw's argument is the OBSERVED acceleration sqrt(y^2+y): the round trip returns y exactly, so h(x) must be evaluated there and nowhere else

   y = g_bar/a0  x = sqrt(y^2+y)  1/h AT y (wrong)  1/h AT x (right)  inflation
       1.00e-06       1.0000e-03         500000.00            500.00    1000.0x
       1.00e-04       1.0000e-02           5000.00             50.01     100.0x
       1.00e-03       3.1639e-02            500.00             15.84      31.6x
       3.70e-03       6.0940e-02            135.14              8.27      16.3x
       1.00e-02       1.0050e-01             50.01              5.07       9.9x
       1.00e-01       3.3166e-01              5.10              1.81       2.8x
       1.00e+00       1.4142e+00              1.12              1.06       1.1x
  [OK] the inflation GROWS as y falls (2.8x at y=0.1 to 1000x at y=1e-6) -- so it is worst exactly where the corpus's liability lives, in the diffuse phase
  deep-regime asymptotics: 1/h AT y -> 1/(2y);  1/h AT x -> 1/(2 sqrt(y)).  Ratio -> 1/sqrt(y).

