====================================================================================================
  Rule applied: a row enters by a MEASURED |a| where one exists, otherwise by its g_bar
  converted through x = sqrt(y^2+y). No row supplies both.
  Baryon allocation as the corpus has it: 10% galaxies, 40% WHIM/filaments, 50% diffuse IGM.

  footing            component                                frac           x    A=1/h   contrib
  canonical rho_DE   galaxies (measured |a|)                  0.10  6.9247e-01     1.23     0.123
  canonical rho_DE   WHIM/filaments (delta=10, R=5 Mpc)       0.40  1.1198e-01     4.58     1.830
  canonical rho_DE   diffuse IGM (delta=0.05, R=300 Mpc)      0.50  6.1071e-02     8.25     4.124
  canonical rho_DE   -> baryon-weighted <1/h>_b                                    6.08
  canonical rho_DE   -> total-matter amplification                                1.797   (budget 1.011 / 1.033)
  alt rho_total      galaxies (measured |a|)                  0.10  5.7359e-01     1.33     0.133
  alt rho_total      WHIM/filaments (delta=10, R=5 Mpc)       0.40  1.0181e-01     5.01     2.005
  alt rho_total      diffuse IGM (delta=0.05, R=300 Mpc)      0.50  5.5565e-02     9.05     4.527
  alt rho_total      -> baryon-weighted <1/h>_b                                    6.66
  alt rho_total      -> total-matter amplification                                1.889   (budget 1.011 / 1.033)

  For comparison, the corpus's banked baryon-weighted figure was ~325 (0.10*3.4 + 0.40*722 + 0.50*135).
  banked <1/h>_b = 356.6;  consistent <1/h>_b = 6.08;  factor 59 smaller
  [OK] under one consistent convention the baryon-weighted amplification is 6.08, not ~357 -- a factor 59 reduction, entirely from evaluating h at the acceleration the framework's own law specifies

====================================================================================================
S6. WHAT THIS BUYS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT
====================================================================================================
  IT BUYS, and this is a genuine reduction of a genuine liability:
   * The diffuse-baryon growth liability drops from a required suppression of order 10^2-10^3
     to order 10^0-10^1. Total-matter amplification 1.80 (canonical) / 1.89 (alt)
     against a budget of 1.011 at 1 sigma and 1.033 at 3 sigma.
   * The 'impossible' framing is withdrawn. A factor of a few is the kind of thing an EFE /
     quadrature argument or a modest regulator can plausibly supply; a factor of 10^3 is not.
   * Combined with the forest collapse (0.4-0.9 sigma on the defensible channel), the
     diffuse-baryon sector is no longer the corpus's sharpest liability. That is now the
     alpha=1 planetary anomaly, which is unaffected by any of this.
  IT DOES NOT BUY:
   * Closure. 1.80 still exceeds 1.033, so the sector is still in tension --
     by a factor 24.5 at 3 sigma on the canonical footing.
   * Any change to the NON-ANALYTICITY objection, which is independent and structural:
     K(z) ~ sqrt(z) at z -> 0, so no Taylor expansion exists at the configuration cosmology
     expands around, and K'(0+) diverges. That argument needs no amplification number at all
     and is untouched by this correction.
   * Any of the galaxy-scale results. Every bound-structure row used a measured |a| and was
     always correct; the RAR's 0.108 dex never depended on h.
  THE HONEST SUMMARY: a correction that runs FOR the framework, of the same kind and found by
  the same method as the three that ran against it today. The regulator is still wanted. It is
  no longer wanted at the 10^3 level, and the reason the old number was 10^3 is that h was
  being asked about an acceleration the theory says matter does not have.
  [OK] the liability is REDUCED but NOT CLOSED: 1.797 > 1.033 at 3 sigma, so this is a repricing, not a rescue
====================================================================================================
